    <!-- Impact-Site-Verification: 65267fd0-0a53-4615-8961-483203ad4f9c -->
    <section class="home-hero">
        <div class="top-note">✦ Chen Laoshi’s Teaching - Toolkit ready-to-use activities and tools for your classroom. ✦</div>
        <div class="hero-content">
            <div class="hero-copy">
                <h1>Chen Laoshi’s<br>Teaching Tools<span>Practical support for every classroom</span></h1>
                <p>A welcoming collection of classroom-ready tools, adaptable activities, and thoughtful teaching ideas for educators across subjects.</p>
                <div class="hero-buttons">
                    <a href="/theme-activities" class="btn">Explore activities</a>
                    <a href="/teaching-tools" class="btn btn-secondary">Open teacher tools</a>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="hero-avatar-wrap">
                <div class="teacher-avatar">
                    <img src="/images/chen-laoshi-logo.svg" alt="Chen Laoshi holding a book, surrounded by sunflowers and classroom supplies">
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <main class="home-paths-section" aria-labelledby="home-paths-heading">
        <div class="home-paths-shell">
            <header class="home-paths-header">
                <div>
                    <div class="eyebrow">Start here</div>
                    <h2 id="home-paths-heading">What would help your class today?</h2>
                </div>
                <p>Build a classroom material, find a tested teaching routine, or explore a classroom item with an honest use case. Choose the kind of support you need today.</p>
            </header>

            <div class="home-paths-grid">
                <article class="home-path-card home-path-card--tools" id="tools">
                    <div class="home-path-card__topline">
                        <span class="home-path-card__number">01 · Teaching Tools</span>
                        <span class="home-path-card__icon" aria-hidden="true">🧰</span>
                    </div>
                    <h3>Build classroom materials you can use right away</h3>
                    <p>Random groups, QR worksheets, spinners, question banks, and review games can support math, science, language arts, social studies, world languages, and more.</p>
                    <ul class="home-path-card__tags" aria-label="Popular teaching tools">
                        <li>Random Groups</li>
                        <li>QR Code</li>
                        <li>Question Banks</li>
                        <li>Review Games</li>
                        <li>Class Spinner</li>
                    </ul>
                    <a href="/teaching-tools" class="home-path-card__link">Open the teaching tools →</a>
                </article>

                <article class="home-path-card home-path-card--resources">
                    <div class="home-path-card__topline">
                        <span class="home-path-card__number">02 · Teaching Resources</span>
                        <span class="home-path-card__icon" aria-hidden="true">📚</span>
                    </div>
                    <h3>Find the teaching method behind the activity</h3>
                    <p>Read clear goals, classroom steps, examples, and adjustment ideas. Chinese-language resources are labeled, and many routines adapt across subjects.</p>
                    <a href="/resources" class="home-path-card__link">Read teaching resources →</a>
                </article>

                <article class="home-path-card home-path-card--recommendations">
                    <div class="home-path-card__recommendation-copy">
                        <span class="home-path-card__number">03 · Classroom Finds</span>
                        <h3>Choose supplies with a repeatable classroom purpose</h3>
                        <p>First find: a 15-drawer rolling classroom organizer.</p>
                        <a href="/recommendations" class="home-path-card__link">See why I recommend it →</a>
                    </div>
                    <img class="home-path-card__product-image" src="/images/15-drawer-rolling-cart.png" alt="Fifteen-drawer rolling classroom organizer" loading="lazy">
                </article>
            </div>

            <div class="home-paths-about">
                <span><strong>New here?</strong> Learn which tools work across subjects and which resources reflect Chen Laoshi's Chinese-language teaching experience.</span>
                <a href="/about">Meet Chen Laoshi →</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </main>

    <section class="content-section content-section--soft" aria-labelledby="latest-resources-heading">
        <div class="content-shell">
            <div class="section-intro" style="padding:0 0 30px; text-align:left; margin:0;">
                <div class="eyebrow">From the teaching resource library</div>
                <h2 id="latest-resources-heading">More than a tool: how to teach with it.</h2>
                <p>Each resource begins with a real classroom goal and includes steps, examples, and the decisions that still belong to the teacher.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="resource-grid home-resource-grid">
                <article class="resource-card">
                    <p class="resource-card__meta">Chinese Language Teaching · 8 min</p>
                    <h2><a href="/resources/chinese-classroom-bingo-five-ways">Five Ways to Use Bingo in Chinese Class</a></h2>
                    <p>Move one Bingo board from recognition and listening to description, follow-up questions, and sentence production.</p>
                    <a class="resource-card__link" href="/resources/chinese-classroom-bingo-five-ways">Read the classroom sequence →</a>
                </article>
                <article class="resource-card">
                    <p class="resource-card__meta">Culture &amp; Celebrations · 7 min</p>
                    <h2><a href="/resources/teaching-mid-autumn-festival-grade-one">Teaching the Mid-Autumn Festival in Grade One</a></h2>
                    <p>A 35-minute lesson with core words, movement, picture sequencing, and room for different family experiences.</p>
                    <a class="resource-card__link" href="/resources/teaching-mid-autumn-festival-grade-one">Read the full lesson →</a>
                </article>
                <article class="resource-card">
                    <p class="resource-card__meta">Vocabulary Instruction · 8 min</p>
                    <h2><a href="/resources/using-word-walls-for-chinese-vocabulary">How to Make a Chinese Word Wall Work</a></h2>
                    <p>Use categories, temporary pinyin support, and five-minute routines so the wall participates in listening, speaking, reading, and writing.</p>
                    <a class="resource-card__link" href="/resources/using-word-walls-for-chinese-vocabulary">Read the teaching guide →</a>
                </article>
            </div>
            <p style="margin:28px 0 0;"><a class="btn" href="/resources">View all teaching resources →</a></p>
        </div>
    </section>

