                <p>Each recommendation explains what students or teachers can do with the item, how it can be reused, and what low-cost alternative could serve the same purpose.</p>
                <a class="btn" href="/recommendations">View classroom finds and disclosures →</a>
            </div>
            <aside class="affiliate-note">
                <h2>Amazon classroom list</h2>
                <p>This is an affiliate link. A qualifying purchase may support the site with a small commission, without increasing your price.</p>
                <a href="https://amzn.to/4qpPByl" target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener noreferrer">Open the Amazon list →</a>
            </aside>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="shop-preview" aria-labelledby="shop-preview-heading">
        <div class="shop-preview-copy">
            <div class="eyebrow">🧲 Classroom finds</div>
            <h2 id="shop-preview-heading">A few joyful classroom helpers.</h2>
            <p>Occasional teacher-friendly supplies, carefully described and ready for a new classroom. The first find: colorful magnetic people for displays, storytelling, and playful language practice.</p>
            <a href="/classroom-shop" class="btn">Visit the chenlaoshi's shop →</a>
            <p class="shop-note">Open-box finds · Shipping included</p>
        </div>
        <img src="/images/magnetic-people-classroom.png" alt="Colorful magnetic people holding classroom artwork on a magnetic board">
    </section>

    <section class="featured">
